menu "Serial screen"

    config MEMTEST_UI_WIDTH
        int "Screen width in columns, borders included"
        default 78
        range 60 200
        help
            The live screen is drawn as a box around MT_UI_ROWS rows. Every
            row occupies this many columns, so the default of 78 produces an
            80-column display that fits a stock 80x24 terminal exactly.

            Widen it if your terminal has more columns, for example 108 for a
            110-column window. If the terminal is narrower than this setting
            each row wraps and the box is destroyed, so the two must be kept
            in step.

endmenu
